  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a downward trend followed by a spike; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10%.",
    "When sentiment history contains a -1.00 reading, the model fails to incorporate immediate downside risk, resulting in significant overestimation of future prices.",
    "Forecasts display extreme lag during high-volatility periods (spikes > 60 EUR), failing to capture the magnitude and duration of sudden price reversals.",
    "The model assumes a smooth linear trajectory that ignores mean reversion; true outcomes frequently oscillate wildly around the forecast path rather than following it.",
    "In scenarios with mixed sentiment (positive and negative spikes), the model defaults to a conservative upward drift, whereas actual market behavior is characterized by sharp corrections."
  ]
}
